degrees of freedom, bipedal locomotion stability under load. Fourth, hardware sophistication: actuator type 
(compliant vs. rigid), onboard sensing, battery runtime. Fifth, software stack depth, proprietary foundation 
models, sim-to-real pipelines, teleoperation-to-autonomy ratio. Sixth, ecosystem partnerships with automotive OEMs,
logistics operators, or manufacturing integrators.\n\nSpecs that companies have not publicly disclosed are noted as
