现有公开资料显示：RoboZaps 的文章宣称其目标是“profiles every major humanoid robot company you need to know in 2026,
including their key robots, funding, pricing, and what makes each one unique”，并以“30+ Humanoid Robot Companies   
Ranked: Who's Winning in 2026”为标题；文章开头指出“Dozens of humanoid robot companies are now                      
racing…”，随后给出“30+”家公司，并反复使用“humanoid robot companies”来描述统计对象；RoboZaps 文中强调如“currently   
being piloted with BMW for automotive manufacturing”“Digit is already working in customer warehouses”“G1 starts at 
$16,000 and is available for purchase today”等表述，将工厂和仓储试点以及可购买状态作为公司描述的关键要素；RoboZaps 
将自身定位为“independent humanoid robot research, reviews, pricing, and buying guidance for operators,             
buyers”。[11]                                                                                                      

现有公开资料显示：PANews 文章写道：“This guide aims to introduce mainstream humanoid robotics companies by 2026,   
covering their main robots, funding situations, pricing, and what makes each company unique.”；文中以“Highest      
Valuation: Figure AI (Valued at $39 billion)”“Lowest price: Yushutech G1                                           
($16,000)”等小节对公司进行比较，显示估值和价格是评估人形机器人公司的重要维度；PANews 文中指出“Largest production   
scale: Tesla (target annual production of 1 million units)”和“First commercial deployment: Agility Robotics        
Digit”，强调量产目标和首个商业部署事件；Forbes 文章标题为“Humanoid Robots: 18 Companies Racing To Build The Next   
Big Thing In AI”，并围绕 18 家人形机器人公司讨论其在工厂、仓库和家庭中的应用前景。[12][13]                         

现有公开资料显示：Forbes 文中提到：“China already has 140 humanoid robot manufacturers and 330 product models by   
2025,” 但随后问道“So, who are the companies leading this race, and which names should business leaders be          
watching?”并给出 18 家公司名单；Humanoid.guide 写道：“A Forbes survey has named 18 humanoid robot companies it sees
as central to the current race for commercial deployment… The useful signal in the roundup is not a single front   
runner. It is the difference between companies with cited factory pilots, production capacity or delivered units,  
and companies still leaning more heavily on demonstrations or long term consumer ambitions.”；Humanoid.guide 将    
Forbes 样本描述为以“factory pilots”“production capacity”“delivered                                                 
units”为依据区分不同公司阶段，并指出这些公司被视为“central to the current race for commercial deployment”；RAISE   
Summit 将自身定位为“the world's leading AI summit, bridging software and hardware (Physical                        
AI/Robotics)”，其博客文章标题为“20 Physical AI Companies to Watch in 2026”。[13][14][15]                           

现有公开资料显示：RAISE 描述 Machina 系列活动为“where robotics and physical AI move from prototypes to             
deployment”，表明其 Physical AI 公司名单关注部署潜力和从原型到落地的过渡；Overview.ai 博客区同时包含“World Models  
and the Next Wave of Industrial Intelligence”和“World Models Explained: How Synthetic Data Trains the Factories of 
the Future”等文章，强调 world models、synthetic data 和工业智能在工厂自动化中的应用；Machina 2026                  
官网上的活动描述为：“The international summit dedicated to humanoids, robotics, industrial autonomy, and           
next-generation human–machine interfaces. MACHINA is built for the people shaping the next generation of robotics  
and physical AI.”；Machina 2026 官网顶部展示赞助方 Logo，包括 Nvidia、OpenAI、Mistral AI、Tesla、Unitree、Hugging  
Face 等，作为活动主要合作品牌。[15][16][17]                                                                        

现有公开资料显示：Machina 2026 网站的 Speakers 部分列出包括 Bernt Børnich（Founder & CEO of 1X）、Jeff             
Cardenas（Co‑founder & CEO of Apptronik）、Agility Robotics 联合创始人以及 Google DeepMind Head of Robotics        
在内的演讲人；Machina 2026 描述该峰会是“where robotics and physical AI move from prototypes to                     
deployment”，强调其主题聚焦从原型走向规模化部署；Between 2021 and 2026, different humanoid and physical AI company 
lists (RoboZaps, PANews/Forbes, RAISE Summit, Overview.ai) deliberately use distinct sampling scopes—humanoid‑only 
vs broader Physical AI, representative subsets vs near‑exhaustive coverage, and inclusion of only companies with   
embodied products vs exclusion of cloud‑only AI providers—so divergent company counts such as 18, 20, or 30+       
reflect differences in statistical definitions rather than factual contradictions.；Forbes’ humanoid robot article 
treats its list of 18 companies as a representative subset of a much larger global and Chinese humanoid ecosystem, 
selecting firms it considers central to the current race for commercial deployment and relevant for business       
leaders, rather than attempting to enumerate all manufacturers.。[17][11][15][16][12][13][14]                      

现有公开资料显示：Forbes’ 18‑company humanoid robot list includes only firms with clearly identified embodied      
humanoid products operating in human environments such as factories, warehouses, and homes, and implicitly excludes
companies that offer only software or cloud AI without their own robot hardware.；RoboZaps’ 2026 humanoid robot    
guide defines its sample as companies with tangible humanoid robot products and positions itself as independent    
research and buying guidance for operators and buyers, aiming to profile ‘every major humanoid robot company’ in   
2026 and ultimately listing more than 30 firms.；RoboZaps and the PANews/Binance Square repost both focus on       
mainstream humanoid robot companies that already have or target real‑world deployment in industrial, logistics, or 
household scenarios, emphasizing factors such as funding, valuation, unit price, production scale targets, and     
first commercial deployments to justify ‘mainstream’ status.；The PANews/Binance Square version of the RoboZaps    
guide restricts its sample to companies with physical humanoid robot products deployed or targeted for industrial, 
logistics, or household use, and does not include firms that only provide cloud AI or simulation platforms without 
their own embodied humanoid robots.。[13][14][11][12]                                                              

现有公开资料显示：Humanoid.guide interprets Forbes’ 18‑company humanoid list as signaling a distinction between    
firms with cited factory pilots, production capacity, or delivered units and those still relying mainly on         
demonstrations or long‑term consumer ambitions, emphasizing deployment maturity as a key implicit selection        
criterion.；RAISE Summit’s ‘20 Physical AI Companies to Watch in 2026’ list defines its sample as broader Physical 
AI and robotics firms, not just humanoid robot companies, and is curated as a media and conference‑organizer       
‘companies to watch’ selection that favors organizations with notable funding, technical novelty, and deployment   
potential.；Overview.ai’s ‘Top 10 Physical AI Companies to Watch in 2026’ list is framed for factory and           
manufacturing contexts and highlights Physical AI companies applying world models, synthetic data, and industrial  
intelligence to automation, reflecting both an industrial‑technology focus and a self‑marketing bias as Overview.ai
includes itself in the top‑10 list.；Machina 2026 positions itself as an international summit dedicated to         
humanoids, robotics, industrial autonomy, and next‑generation human–machine interfaces, emphasizing the transition 
of robotics and Physical AI from prototypes to deployment and featuring major ecosystem players as sponsors and    
speakers (including Nvidia, OpenAI, Mistral AI, Tesla, Unitree, Hugging Face, 1X, Apptronik, Agility Robotics, and 
Google DeepMind).。[14][15][16][17]                                                                                

