Tesla Optimus and Figure’s robots as general-labor or manufacturing-collaboration platforms, and Digit as a        
warehouse-focused humanoid.；Multiple sources report that the global embodied AI market size is projected to reach 
about USD 4.44 billion by 2025 with high expected compound growth, and that 2026 is viewed by some investment      
analysts as a potential inflection point for humanoid robots and embodied AI due to labor shortages, aging         
populations, manufacturing automation needs and advances in large models and simulation.。[19][18][22]             

