现有公开资料显示：In China’s humanoid robot industrial applications (notably automotive manufacturing and consumer 
electronics), deployments as of 2025–early 2026 remain largely at pilot verification stage with small‑batch orders,
whereas non‑humanoid embodied robots in logistics, special inspection, and hotel services have already achieved    
hundred‑ to thousand‑unit commercial orders.；Leading Chinese humanoid robot and embodied intelligence companies   
highlighted in recent industry reports include Unitree Robotics, Zhiyuan Robotics, Galaxy General, Yunshenchu      
Technology, Qinglang Intelligence, Digital Huaxia, and others, which together form a representative first tier of  
commercial players.；Industry analyses distinguish two main commercialization routes for embodied humanoid robot   
companies: (1) a general‑purpose humanoid platform route, where once a common platform is validated, cross‑scenario
replication leads to strong Matthew effects favoring scale players; and (2) a vertical‑scenario specialist route,  
where firms first achieve a closed commercial loop in a single high‑value scenario, using cash flow and scenario   
data to reinforce core technology and then expand to other scenarios.；Embodied intelligence (具身智能) is defined 
in Chinese research policy documents as AI fused with physical entities, with robots identified as one of the      
hottest carriers, and humanoid robots and non‑humanoid robots classified as two major categories within            
robot‑focused embodied intelligence.。[27][25][28][24][26]                                                         

